1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Give me a break, that excuse is ridiculous, and everyone has already waited thirty minutes for the missing driver.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:19,000
You should get a life instead of spending every evening counting strangers who liked a photo on your phone.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:29,000
What the heck happened to this kitchen, because the flour covers every chair and nobody remembers making any bread.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:39,000
I am all ears while you explain the unexpected message, because the situation sounds much stranger than yesterday.

5
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:49,000
Please hang in there during this difficult week, because your friends will support you until the exams are finished.

6
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:59,000
You bet, I can help tomorrow, and I will bring enough boxes for the books and the kitchen equipment.

7
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:09,000
Fair enough, I understand why you refused the invitation after discovering that the organizer changed the ticket price.

8
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:19,000
No way, I refuse to lend you my bicycle again after you returned it yesterday with a damaged wheel.

9
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:29,000
Not a chance, the team cannot finish an entire film tonight when the camera battery is completely empty.

10
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:39,000
We are fed up with the constant noise from that restaurant, especially when the music continues after midnight.

11
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:49,000
The teenagers mess around during rehearsal instead of practicing, although the audience will arrive within another hour.

12
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:59,000
Do not screw up this final payment, because another wrong account number would delay the project for several days.

13
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:09,000
After another dishonest excuse, our unreliable colleague is on thin ice with the manager who previously defended him.

14
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:19,000
In a nutshell, the new schedule gives everyone longer breaks and reduces the number of meetings during the morning.

15
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:29,000
Those concert tickets cost an arm and a leg, so we decided to listen to the broadcast from home.

16
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:39,000
I must bite the bullet and arrange the dental appointment, although I have avoided that conversation for months.

17
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:49,000
The failed experiment leaves us back to square one, and we must design a completely different method next week.

18
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:59,000
That unnecessary insult was the last straw, and our patient coordinator finally decided to resign from the committee.

19
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:09,000
Your spare camera could save the day because our photographer discovered a serious technical problem before the ceremony.

20
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:19,000
Please do not beat around the bush, because we need a clear answer about the missing money before lunch.

21
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:29,000
We will burn the midnight oil tonight to finish the application before the scholarship deadline tomorrow morning.

22
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:39,000
I might get cold feet before the performance, even though I have rehearsed the same music for several weeks.

23
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:49,000
The cancelled interview was a blessing in disguise because it allowed me to accept a much better offer later.

24
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:59,000
I have second thoughts about joining the tour after discovering that the company ignores several important safety rules.

25
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:09,000
The supervisor should not turn a blind eye to repeated bullying simply because the employee sells many products.

26
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:19,000
This excellent presentation will raise the bar for the remaining speakers, who now have a difficult example to match.

27
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:29,000
I cannot keep a straight face when the actor delivers that absurd speech while wearing a giant paper crown.

28
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:39,000
Our youngest teammate is on cloud nine after receiving the scholarship that her family thought was almost impossible.

29
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:49,000
Winning the competition is a long shot, but the experience would help us understand the weaknesses in our design.

30
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:59,000
We need to think outside the box because the usual advertising methods have produced disappointing results for months.

31
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:09,000
You should sleep on it before accepting the expensive contract, because a calmer decision tomorrow might protect your savings.

32
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:19,000
Please pull yourself together before the interview, because you know the material and deserve the same respect as everyone.

33
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:29,000
The documents back up her explanation of the accident, although the witness originally described a very different sequence.

34
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:39,000
We cannot put up with this unreliable service forever, especially when the company charges more than every competitor.

35
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:49,000
Our new accountant works by the book and refuses to approve expenses without the required receipts and signatures.

36
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:59,000
The festival was a mixed bag because the music was excellent but the food was cold and expensive.

37
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:09,000
I am on edge before the medical appointment, although the nurse explained that the examination should be routine.

38
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:19,000
Does that surname ring a bell, because I think the woman studied with us during the first summer course.

39
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:29,000
The captain must face the music after admitting that he ignored the safety report before the dangerous voyage.

40
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:39,000
The children will go bananas when they discover the puppy, but we should explain the responsibilities before any celebration.

41
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:49,000
The skating instructor stood on thin ice near the shore, where the frozen water measured only two centimeters.

42
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:59,000
The historical demonstration used a lantern to burn the midnight oil that the merchant had bottled for night lighting.

43
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:09,000
The sculptor used two rulers to keep a straight face on the wooden block instead of carving a curved surface.

44
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:19,000
The technician used a jack to raise the bar above the machine, allowing the heavy metal rod to move vertically.

45
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:29,000
The film director requested a long shot that showed the whole hillside, rather than a close view of the actor.

46
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:39,000
The robot designer could turn a blind eye toward the wall by rotating the damaged camera that no longer detected light.

47
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:49,000
My brother might want to read the blue report after breakfast, although the teacher did not require any extra homework.

48
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:59,000
The speaker described a really ordinary room containing six chairs, a small table and a cabinet beside the window.

49
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:09,000
There were three yellow chairs beside the desk, but their owner could not remember which shop originally sold them.

50
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:19,000
Please open the red box containing yesterday's envelopes, because I need the receipt that arrived with the replacement cable.

51
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:29,000
The comfortable lamp makes studying easier during dark evenings, although good lighting cannot replace preparation for a difficult examination.

52
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:39,000
You should not forget any appointments tomorrow, because your calendar contains several meetings that cannot easily be rearranged.

53
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:49,000
The notebook contained eighteen pages of measurements, and the assistant checked every number before signing the laboratory record.

54
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:59,000
A short announcement explained the timetable, while the passengers waited quietly beside a row of wooden seats near the entrance.

55
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:09,000
The artist selected a blue pencil and drew a narrow line between the two circles printed on the paper.

56
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:19,000
The visitor described an empty apartment with white walls, a wooden door and several windows overlooking the quiet street.

57
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:29,000
Our cousin bought twelve envelopes and wrote the addresses carefully before placing the stamps beside the new telephone.

58
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:39,000
The teacher showed a diagram containing four arrows, then asked the class to describe the direction of each arrow.

59
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:49,000
The envelope contained a receipt and a handwritten note confirming the date of the next meeting at the central office.

60
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:59,000
A small photograph showed the old station before renovation, with two bicycles leaning against the wall beside the ticket window.
